# ==== T-FMT-C · author blanks BETWEEN DEFINITIONS nested in a `meta if` block
#
# `format_module` preserves an author blank between TOP-LEVEL items and
# `format_block_stmts` preserves one between statements. The nested-ITEM loops —
# the bodies of `meta if` / `elif` / `else` — were the one member of that family
# with no such check, so a platform backend wrapped in
# `meta if platform() == "macos":` came back with every definition welded to the
# next. One real file lost 88 blank lines this way.
#
# All three branch bodies now route through ONE producer,
# `Formatter::format_nested_items`, rather than three copies of the loop: three
# copies were three chances to omit the check, and one of them omitting it is
# exactly this snag. `formatter_child_collection_loop_census` in tests/lints.rs
# pins that there is one.
#
# AXIS (4 cells): blank between nested defs in the `then` branch · in an `elif`
#   branch · in the `else` branch · no blank stays absent (the `frame_begin` /
#   `frame_end` pair in the `elif` branch). The fifth cell of the axis — a RUN
#   of blanks collapsing to one — cannot live in a fixpoint fixture, since its
#   whole point is that input and output differ; it is
#   `meta_if_nested_item_blank_run.gg` with an `.expected` companion.
#
# SECOND AXIS (2 cells, the CLAUSE face of the same item-level block): a blank
#   ABOVE the item-level `elif:` and above the item-level `else:`. Those headers
#   are not items, so the nested-item loop cannot see a blank above them — the
#   identical reason a statement-level clause header needs its own check. ⚠ The
#   anchor for the item-level `else` has to be DERIVED (walk back from the first
#   item's start to the clause's colon): the first item's start sits one line
#   below the header, so using it directly reports the `else:` line itself as
#   the content above and every author blank reads as absent.
#
# Same rule as both siblings: a blank iff the author wrote one, runs collapse to
# one, and the FIRST item of a branch never gets one (a blank between a block
# opener and its first item is sparseness, not paragraphing) — which is why
# `frame_begin` sits directly under the `meta if` header here.
#
# RED pre-fix (recorded 2026-08-11): every blank cell lost its blank and the
#   definitions came out contiguous. The run-collapse and no-blank cells were
#   GREEN — BREAK-AND-WATCH: emit `blank_line()` unconditionally in
#   `format_nested_items` and the no-blank pair REDs with a blank the author
#   never wrote.

meta if platform() == "macos":
    int backend_id():
        return 1

    int frame_begin():
        return 2

    int frame_end():
        return 3

elif platform() == "windows":
    int backend_id():
        return 10

    int frame_begin():
        return 20
    int frame_end():
        return 30

else:
    int backend_id():
        return 100

    int frame_begin():
        return 200

    int frame_end():
        return 300

void main():
    print(backend_id())
    print(frame_begin())
    print(frame_end())
